  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nLab\ntokens-to-css\n\n// Tool\n\ntokens-to-css \n\nTurns a design token file into typed CSS custom properties, with dark mode built in.\n\nView the repo\nstars\n410\ndownloads\n6,300\nlicense\nMIT\nInstall\nCopy\nnpm install -D tokens-to-css\n\n\nREADME.md\nMIT\n\ntokens-to-css reads the token file your design tool exports and writes three things from it: CSS custom properties, a typed TypeScript map and a variables file the design library can import back.\n\nUsage\nbash\nCopy\nnpx tokens-to-css tokens.json --out src/tokens\n\ncss\nCopy\n:root {\n\n  --color-ground: #0b0c0e;\n\n  --color-accent: #c6ff3d;\n\n  --space-4: 16px;\n\n}\n\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {\n\n  :root { --color-ground: #f6f6f1; }\n\n}\n\nDetails\nAliases are resolved, and kept as var() references where that is useful\nDark and light modes come from token sets, not from duplicated files\nThe TypeScript map makes a typo in a token name a compile error\n\nIn this readme\n\n01\nUsage\n02\nDetails\nKind\nTool\nLicense\nMIT\nRepository\ngithub.com\nMore from the lab. \n06\nEverything in the lab\nExperiment · 320 stars\nshader-notes\nForty small WebGL sketches, each one under fifty lines and explained line by line.\nLibrary · 2,140 stars\nuse-latency\nA React hook that measures how long every interaction really takes, in production.\nExperiment · 1,260 stars\nglyphfield\nDraws any picture as source code on a canvas. It runs the portrait at the top of this site.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n17:01 CEST\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.\n\nEdit Content",
